Feature: Required declaration-bound enum choices preserve all released members
  Scenario: BOOLEAN and LOGICAL have explicit typed choices without an implicit value
    Given a complete original complex direct tuple with required SameSense or ClosedCurve unset
    When the caller chooses a declared T, F or U option from the original resident control
    Then only the matching complete enum payload fills its exact target index
    And all supplied sibling aggregates and attributes stay exact through central diff and inverse
  Scenario: The complete 53-member and 34-member domains use genuine source-owned pages
    Given a required IfcDerivedUnit.UnitType or IfcSensorType.PredefinedType field
    When the caller navigates both 31-member windows through original page bindings
    Then the union of visible options contains every released member
    And each page contains at most 32 options including at most one declared current selection
    And navigation changes only page metadata and generation, preserving source and command arguments
    When the caller chooses USERDEFINED or NOTDEFINED on the last page
    Then the same strict candidate and original central mutation authority emits exact output and inverse
  Scenario: A rootless unchanged-type repair preserves the original required Elements aggregate
    Given IfcDerivedUnit has matching static direct and full attribute count and the same canonical requested type
    When caller UnitType fills its original required Unset slot
    Then original Elements, UserDefinedType and Name remain exact and no default or aggregate is generated
    And inherited-layout simple conversion or a different requested type is refused
  Scenario: Page and declaration authority remains original
    Given current source, profile, revision, request and resident generation
    When a page path, offset, token or revision is substituted
    Then it cannot authorize another field or a model mutation
    And cancellation, denied axes and posting refusal retain all partial choice rows and payloads for original retirement

  Scenario: An earlier required choice preserves an invalid UTF8 sibling draft
    Given a later logical input contains the exact neutral multibyte draft text
    When the caller chooses U for an earlier missing logical input
    Then the resident fixed binding retains sorted target indices and every sibling UTF8 byte
    And readiness stays false without promoting the unknown raw word to a declared option
  Scenario: Unchanged type completion emits no name scaffolding
    Given the original declaration and direct-layout proof admit an unchanged type repair
    When required caller choices complete its strict candidate tuple
    Then the central batch contains only actual changed SetEntityArg atoms
    And the inverse restores original unset slots without any identity SetEntityName atom
    And page coordinates identify candidate target attributes independently of raw input row ordinals
